outputs.exact_statement:
Let $D\subset\mathbb R^2$ be compact, let $V$ be $C^1$ on an open neighborhood of $D$, and let $L,h>0$. Suppose that $$\label{b:main-condition}
 \operatorname{tr}DV(p)=0,\qquad -L^{-2}<\det DV(p)\le0
 \quad(p\in D).$$ For every $\varepsilon>0$, there are finitely many compact nondegenerate square tiles $T_i\subset\mathbb R^2$, with possibly different orientations, and velocities $g_i\in\mathbb R^2$ such that $$\label{b:main-cover}
 E(D,V,L)\subset\bigcup_i\mathcal C(T_i,g_i),\qquad
 \sum_i |T_i|J_h(g_i)
 \le\int_D J_h(V(p))\,dp+\varepsilon.$$ Under $F_h$, the perpendicular bases are compact nondegenerate parallelograms and have total area $h\sum_i|T_i|J_h(g_i)$. No condition on the area of $\partial D$ or smallness of $\|DV\|$ is required.

Let $L>0$ and let $A$ be a real $2\times2$ matrix satisfying $$\operatorname{tr}A=0,\qquad -L^{-2}<\det A\le0.$$ Fix $p_0,v_0\in\mathbb R^2$ and write $W(p)=v_0+A(p-p_0)$. There is an orthonormal basis $e_1,e_2$ such that, for every $\tau>0$, the lattice $$\Lambda=p_0+\tau\mathbb Ze_1+\tau\mathbb Ze_2$$ and its closed squares $$T_l=l+[-\tau/2,\tau/2]e_1+[-\tau/2,\tau/2]e_2
 \qquad(l\in\Lambda)$$ satisfy $$\mathbb R^2=\bigcup_{l\in\Lambda}\bigl(T_l+sW(l)\bigr)
 \qquad(|s|\le L).$$ If $x$ belongs to the translated tile indexed by $l$, then $|x-l-sW(l)|\le\tau$. Furthermore, $$\label{b:affine-inverse}
 \|(I+sA)^{-1}\|
 \le \frac{1+L\|A\|}{1+L^2\det A}
 \qquad(|s|\le L),$$ where the norm is the Euclidean operator norm.
